7. CLI NOTE -- THE `no` FORMS DO NOT MIRROR THE `set` FORMS
-------------------------------------------------------------
Teardown hit this and it is worth recording for anyone scripting a restore:

  no auth-web-server ping-poll type arp        -> % Invalid input detected at '^' marker.
  no auth-web-server ping-poll type            -> accepted
  no auth-web-server ping-poll interval 10     -> rejected;  no ... interval       -> accepted
  no auth-web-server ping-poll failcount 3     -> rejected;  no ... failcount      -> accepted
  no auth-web-server ipaddress 10.38.22.34     -> rejected;  no ... ipaddress      -> accepted

i.e. the negation takes NO argument where the positive form requires one.  Because `cfg.py`
stops at the first `% ` line, a teardown batch written by mirroring the setup lines aborts at the
first of these and silently leaves everything after it in place.  Each `no` was therefore issued
in its own invocation and its result checked individually.


